course: dictionary
lesson: 9423
title: Squirrels and hidden food
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A squirrel is a small furry animal with a long bushy tail. It lives in trees, eats nuts and seeds, and can climb and jump very well. Scientists call squirrels rodents and mammals.
explain: In autumn, many squirrels bury nuts to eat in winter. «Grey squirrels bury thousands of nuts in autumn, each in a different place, and find many by memory and smell.»
explain: Squirrels can also squirrel away food. That means to hide or save things to use later. It is an informal phrase, so you would use it in a story or a chat, not in a science report.
explain: Wild squirrels can bite, so do not feed them or try to touch them. Enjoy watching them from a safe distance.
fact: A squirrel is a small furry animal with a long bushy tail.
fact: «Squirrels and jays bury acorns and nuts for winter and forget many, which grow into new trees.»
fact: One jay can bury several thousand acorns in a single autumn.
fact: In Britain, the grey squirrel from America has replaced most native red squirrels.
fact: «Squirrel away» is informal and means to hide or save things to use later.
exercise: What is a squirrel? | *A small furry animal with a long bushy tail that lives in trees | A tree that grows nuts in winter | A large grey bird that catches fish
exercise: «Grey squirrels bury thousands of nuts in autumn, each in a different place.» Why do they do this? | To make the tree fall over | *To save food for later in winter | To decorate the ground | To keep warm in summer
exercise: Ella says, «He squirrelled away his pocket money.» What does squirrel away mean? | *To hide or save something to use later | To spend it all at once | To throw it away | To give it to a friend
test: Why can a buried nut grow into a new tree? | *Because some nuts are forgotten and left in the ground | Because nuts only grow in shops | Because squirrels water them every day | Because the sun melts the shell at once
test: Why should you not feed wild squirrels? | Because they are never hungry | *Because they can bite | Because they do not eat nuts | Because they are too big to eat
exam: Where did the grey squirrel come from, and what did it do to red squirrels in Britain? | Canada, where it made red squirrels rare in trees | *America, where it replaced most red squirrels | Scotland, where it helped red squirrels grow | Australia, where it made red squirrels bigger
